Except that 'y' doesn't count as a letter when determining if there's a
cmavo cluster, and "D's thread" is {le dy. clita}. Written or not, the
pause after the 'y' is required.


On Thu, May 29, 2014 at 7:39 PM, Pierre Abbat <phma@bezitopo.org> wrote:

> On Thursday, May 29, 2014 14:03:39 Jonathan Jones wrote:
> > cmavo clusters never have consonant clusters, lujvo always do.
>
> Not quite. A lujvo can contain a sequence of a consonant, 'y', and a
> consonant. So can a cmavo cluster.
>
> ledycilta (hypha)
> le dycilta (D's thread, but some parsers may choke)
> ledy cilta (D's thread)
> lekybumoi (the Qth, I think valfendi chokes on this)
> lekybumru (cold fog)
